From 78f2f0a85501d6c32ce9fcfc8e7e83776c2b0524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:27:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(post)!: Air coolant mode, machine default coolant,
 editor keeps coolant codes

An operation can ask for Air (CoolantMode::Air, PARAM Coolant air): every
post that reads the ask resolves it from the machine's Air / Air blast
entry, or refuses it by name. carvera.cps now declares coolantModes and
posts the op's ask instead of "the first Flood entry", so a profile that
kept the seeded Flood M8 beside an Air M7 no longer posts M8 for air.
tormach.cps takes the generic flood law (no air/mist code for a flood
op). A new op starts on its machine's default coolant (Air on an
Air-only Carvera). The machine file editor adds a coolant with its code,
can remove any coolant (the seeded Flood included), lays its controls
out so a narrow pane never clips them, and refuses a codeless coolant by
name before any save.

BREAKING CHANGE: a Flood op on a machine whose only coolant is Air (an
op on the shipped Carvera saved before this change) is refused by name
instead of posting the air code M7; pick Air for the op.

Fixes #869

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
